<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  RUT_TibannaGas.xml                     UtinniPatches · FORGE_MECHANICS_1 F2
  ============================================================================
  forge_kit_spec.md F2 "beldon herds + the tibanna harvest" (§4, §7, ban 5).
  "There is no other tibanna on the planet" — this ThingDef is the ONLY
  source: produced exclusively by RM_CompGatherableGas (the F2 spike's
  already-compiling comp, RUT_TibannaTap_BeldonWiring.xml this same pass
  attaches it to RSW_Beldon). Ban 5's own linter check ("no RecipeDef
  products, no butcher yield, no trader-stock tag outside Imperial hands")
  applies to THIS def by construction: it appears in no <products> of any
  RecipeDef, no ThingDef's <butcherProducts>, and no TraderKindDef's stock
  generator anywhere in this repo — verified by repo-wide grep this same
  pass (see FORGE_MECHANICS_1.md's own build-pass write-up for the exact
  command and result). Trade wiring is explicitly TIBANNA_EMBARGO_PLOT_1's
  job, not this file's.

  Plain resource good, no comps of its own — same shape as RUT_WickStem.xml
  (SUMP_MECHANICS_1 S5): the gathering comp lives on the ANIMAL, not the
  item, so the item itself needs nothing beyond ResourceBase.

  MarketValue is an explicit INVENTED PLACEHOLDER, not a real pricing call —
  TIBANNA_EMBARGO_PLOT_1 owns the real figure (a planet-wide monopoly good
  should price accordingly; left non-zero only so the def is legally
  tradeable rather than reading as worthless in the interim).

  🔴 Texture: intended to reuse vanilla Chemfuel's own icon
  (Things/Item/Resource/Chemfuel) as a pressurized-gas placeholder, same
  "borrow the nearest legible vanilla icon" practice RUT_WickStem.xml
  established — but validate_patch.py flags that choice as a hard ERROR
  ("'things/' IS this mod's own texture namespace"), because UtinniPatches
  already ships its own Things/Item/* tree elsewhere, so its own-namespace
  heuristic cannot tell a deliberate cross-mod reuse from a typo in this
  mod's own art. Rather than ship a disputed claim with no live game access
  to settle it, this def points at its OWN new texPath instead
  (Things/Item/Resource/RUT_TibannaGas) and is held via src/DEPLOY_HOLD.txt
  until art lands — same shape as every other new-art hold in this build
  pass (RUT_VentSmelter/Kiln/Forge, RUT_DeadCreep, RUT_DyingCreep).

  Flammability 0.5, not Chemfuel's 2.0 and no CompProperties_Explosive: raw
  tibanna gas is a contained industrial commodity in this kit's own telling
  (metered by the Empire, tapped like shearing), not a walking incendiary —
  the volatility framing belongs to refined chemfuel, not this good.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Defs>

  <ThingDef ParentName="ResourceBase">
    <defName>RUT_TibannaGas</defName>
    <label>tibanna gas</label>
    <description>Pressurized gas tapped from a living beldon, like shearing. There is no other source of it on the planet — the Empire's own station exists to meter this.</description>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Item/Resource/RUT_TibannaGas</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_StackCount</graphicClass>
    </graphicData>
    <statBases>
      <MarketValue>10</MarketValue>
      <MaxHitPoints>50</MaxHitPoints>
      <Mass>0.03</Mass>
      <Flammability>0.5</Flammability>
      <DeteriorationRate>0.5</DeteriorationRate>
    </statBases>
    <stackLimit>75</stackLimit>
    <thingCategories>
      <li>ResourcesRaw</li>
    </thingCategories>
  </ThingDef>

</Defs>
